\\_doc”:{“steps”:\\[{“pace”:{“end”:376,“start”:330,“units”:“secs/km”},“duration”:600},{“reps”:2,“text”:“2x”,“steps”:\\[{“pace”:{“end”:230,“start”:210,“units”:“secs/km”},“distance”:1000,“duration”:220},{“pace”:{“end”:360,“start”:310,“units”:“secs/km”},“duration”:120}\\],“distance”:2720.430107526882,“duration”:680},{“pace”:{“end”:376,“start”:330,“units”:“secs/km”},“duration”:600}\\],“locales”:\\[\\],“options”:{},“distance”:6134.356606559764,“duration”:1880,“strain\\_score”:null,“average\\_watts”:0,“normalized\\_power”:0,“variability\\_index”:null,“polarization\\_index”:null},“push\\_errors”:null,“athlete\\_cannot\\_edit”:false,“hide\\_from\\_athlete”:false,“structure\\_read\\_only”:false,“created\\_by\\_id”:“i611360”,“shared\\_event\\_id”:null,“entered”:false,“carbs\\_per\\_hour”:null,“sub\\_type”:null,“distance”:6134.3564,“tags”:null,“attachments”:null,“oauth\\_client\\_id”:null,“external\\_id”:“limiar-2x1km-pace-002”,“load\\_target”:null,“time\\_target”:null,“distance\\_target”:null,“training\\_availability”:“NORMAL”,“max\\_training\\_time”:null,“can\\_train\\_sports”:null,“plan\\_athlete\\_id”:null,“plan\\_folder\\_id”:null,“plan\\_workout\\_id”:null,“plan\\_applied”:null,“icu\\_intensity”:null,“strain\\_score”:null,“plan\\_name”:null} **%** marcosreno@MBAReno backend %\n\nThe `workout_doc` looks correct. However, when I open the workout on my Garmin, I only see the duration. The pace range is missing. Is the `pace` field in `workout_doc` supposed to be converted to a pace target when the workout is pushed to Garmin? The same problem when upload a FIT file."}
{"role":"assistant","content":"Both sources agree: the native Intervals target shape is `start`–`end` (the forum readback shows `\"pace\": {\"end\": 376, \"start\": 330, \"units\": \"secs/km\"}`), and the Worklore article documents that `value`–`end` is what triggers zone-mapping on the watch. The fix is a one-word rename in `hr_target`.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_aqzv4HDwZA36FWSRwUbQC1rK","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"gen.py\",\"old_string\":\"    lo, hi = step[\\\"hr_pct\\\"]\\n    return {\\\"units\\\": \\\"%lthr\\\", \\\"value\\\": lo, \\\"end\\\": hi}\",\"new_string\":\"    lo, hi = step[\\\"hr_pct\\\"]\\n    return {\\\"units\\\": \\\"%lthr\\\", \\\"start\\\": lo, \\\"end\\\": hi}\"}"}}]}
